In mathematics, the omega symbol is written as lowercase (ω) or uppercase (Ω). 
It represents various concepts depending on the field, including the smallest infinite ordinal number in set theory (ω), an asymptotic lower bound in computer science (Ω), and a variable domain region in calculus (ω).


